WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.113
- All right lets close up this hour

00:00:01.113 --> 00:00:03.570
with one more story to brighten your day.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.959
This is, What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.959 --> 00:00:07.620
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.140
A Georgia man has collected
tens of thousands of dollars

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.970
to help random strangers $1 at a time.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.400
In 2018, he started what
he calls $1 Thursday.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.240
It's a simple social media campaign

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.900
in which he asks friends, family,

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.900
and neighbors to donate a buck

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.930
on any given Thursday to lend a hand

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.480
to others who are struggling.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.890
It's had a major impact
on his entire community.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.920
Let's get this do-gooder on the line.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.010
Watching on WSB TV, Atlanta at 10:00 AM,

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.447
What's up Anthony?

00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:35.460
(audience clapping)

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.973
- What's up Kelly, how's it going?

00:00:36.973 --> 00:00:40.370
- Oh men its going all
right, well happy Thursday.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.907
- Well thank you and likewise.

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:43.880
- How did all this begin?

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.760
- Well, actually in 2018,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.150
I ran into a classmate of mine

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.550
and I noticed that she
just didn't look herself.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.420
She gave me a little bit of background

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.250
on struggles she's had.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.680
And I couldn't just walk away

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.680
and not think about it.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.270
So over in the night,

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.780
I heard this voice saying $1, Thursday.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.110
And honestly, it freaked me out,

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.080
but I was like, okay, this is God.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.730
I started to type on Facebook, I posted it

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.250
basically saying a young lady needs help,

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.410
need the community to the rally behind.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.990
Once I posted it, it was
just like, boom she sent $2.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.530
She had no idea this was about her.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.430
And in the midst of receiving that $2,

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:22.900
it turned into one 20 real quick.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.890
I was able to buy groceries,

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.640
I was able to give her a $50

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.410
for getting her nails done,

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:30.560
even give her a little bit of gas money.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.397
And the warmth that I felt

00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:33.530
was just through the roof

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.420
like she teared up, she hugged me.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.090
It was a great day.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:38.923
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:38.923 --> 00:01:41.180
It's a beautiful thing to take
care of someone like that.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.400
Thank you so much for sharing

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.233
this story with us.

00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:45.470
Can you tell us about just
some of the other people

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:46.560
that you may have helped?

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.030
- Yes, this time last year, I actually,

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.440
we had a gentleman in town
that had a house fire.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.440
He lost his wife and
two kids in this fire.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.470
I saw it via Facebook.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.167
So I pulled $100 out of my pocket

00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:00.000
and I was like, you know what,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.180
we gotta get behind them,

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:02.480
we have to do something.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.900
Within 24 hours it raised $8,000.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.620
From there, I went into food systems,

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.500
I started to do sneakers for kids

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.410
that might need 'em,

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:14.490
or just needed a little pick me up.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.600
Gift baskets for teachers.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.340
And I also had a run in with

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.280
the guy who had COVID here in Troup County

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.570
he was the first case.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.340
And I was able to bless him with $2,200

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.590
when he came home and the community today

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:29.730
literally got behind it and supported it.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.530
- Oh my gosh! You have such a great heart.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.440
Thank you so much for
being such a great example

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.740
of how we all should live
our daily lives Anthony.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.040
This is a beautiful
thing that you're doing

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.680
for so man people out there.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.080
I'm liking your posts
right now, all right?

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.690
- All right, thank you.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.400
- All right, well that's not all.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.940
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen makers

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.920
of FriXion the go-to erasable pen

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.180
of The Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.300
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly,

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.133
just like you.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.930
So they're gonna give you $1000.

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:55.819
How's that sound?

00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:56.897
- Gosh, wow! Thank you.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.210
- Yeah, thank you so much Anthony.

